IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), piece ei2: the nouns this piece declares.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- Nothing here is a rule. Four enumerations that more than one of the ei2 modules, or a module and
-- the seat layer, need to share. The persons and offices are the keel's (`Party` in eia-core), the
-- reasons for benefits are the keel's (`Reason for benefits`), and a period of days is the keel's.
-- Every name begins with ei2 so that it cannot clash with another piece's.

§ `The kinds of employment support measure`

-- s 59 says the Commission "may establish employment support measures ... including measures to"
-- do four things. The list is open ("including"), so a fifth constructor stands for a measure that is
-- none of the four. Sections 25(1), 26 and 5(1)(e) of the Act key on "paragraph 59(a)", "59(c) or (d)".
-- src:1072 | 59 The Commission may establish employment support measures to help insured participants and other workers, including workers in groups underrepresented in the labour market, to obtain or keep employment, including measures to
-- src:1073 | (a) provide insured participants with courses or programs of instruction or training;
-- src:1074 | (b) provide insured participants with employment opportunities or provide employment support;
-- src:1075 | (c) provide workers with employment assistance services; and
-- src:1076 | (d) support research, innovation or partnerships related to helping workers to prepare for, obtain or keep employment and to be productive participants in the labour market.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 59 (src:1072-1076)
DECLARE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure` IS ONE OF
    `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training`
    `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support`
    `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`
    `ei2 s 59(d) measure supporting research, innovation or partnerships`
    `ei2 an employment support measure not described in paragraphs 59(a) to (d)`

§ `How the weeks of benefits are divided between claimants`

-- s 23.3(6): the remaining weeks "may be divided in the manner agreed to by those claimants. If they cannot
-- agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules."
-- src:671 | (6) If a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.062 in respect of the same adult, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 152.062 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 15 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by those claimants. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(6) (src:671)
DECLARE `ei2 Way of dividing the weeks` IS ONE OF
    `ei2 divided in the manner the claimants agreed`
    `ei2 divided in accordance with the prescribed rules`

§ `The grounds of disqualification under section 27`

-- s 27(1)(a) to (d) and 27(1.1) are the five grounds; s 28(1) sets a different number of weeks
-- for each (7 to 12 for (a) and (b); at most 6 for (c), (d) and (1.1)).
-- src:710 | 27 (1) A claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under this Part if, without good cause since the interruption of earnings giving rise to the claim, the claimant
-- src:711 | (a) has not applied for a suitable employment that is vacant after becoming aware that it is vacant or becoming vacant, or has failed to accept the employment after it has been offered to the claimant;
-- src:712 | (b) has not taken advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment;
-- src:713 | (c) has not carried out a written direction given to the claimant by the Commission with a view to assisting the claimant to find suitable employment, if the direction was reasonable having regard both to the claimant’s circumstances and to the usual means of obtaining that employment; or
-- src:714 | (d) has not attended an interview that the Commission has directed the claimant to attend to enable the Commission or another appropriate agency
-- src:715 | (i) to provide information and instruction to help the claimant find employment, or
-- src:716 | (ii) to identify whether the claimant might be assisted by job training or other employment assistance.
-- src:718 | (1.1) A claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under this Part if
-- src:719 | (a) the Commission or an authority that the Commission designates has, with the agreement of the claimant, referred the claimant to a course or program of instruction or training or to any other employment activity for which assistance has been provided under an employment support measure other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c); and
-- src:720 | (b) the Commission has terminated the referral because
-- src:721 | (i) without good cause, the claimant has not attended or participated in the course, program or employment activity and, in the opinion of the Commission, it is unlikely that the claimant will successfully complete the course, program or employment activity,
-- src:722 | (ii) without good cause, the claimant has withdrawn from the course, program or employment activity, or
-- src:723 | (iii) the organization providing the course, program or employment activity has expelled the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 27(1), s 27(1.1) (src:710-716) (src:718-723)
DECLARE `ei2 Ground of disqualification under section 27` IS ONE OF
    `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment`
    `ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment`
    `ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission`
    `ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission`
    `ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated`
